  "materialNarrowings": {
    "S2": "Independent verification is strongest when a discrete evaluator/admission mechanism or replicable test exists. Broad explanatory science can progress through distributed criticism and accumulating evidence without one independent decisive verifier.",
    "S3": "HD2 reinforces HD1 narrowing: generalization binds the declared applicability scope. It also adds temporal/lifecycle generalization—1858 cable first contact, Bessemer spectacular conversion and atmospheric railway operation all show that a successful moment is not durable general performance.",
    "S5": "Unlike HD1, HD2 contains clearer non-Agent instances: Rothamsted treatment histories/samples, Nightingale decision-grade statistical records, chemistry atomic-weight conventions and international regulations. These support durable structured state in information-rich institutions, but not a universal requirement for every physical innovation.",
    "S6": "HD2 narrows cost repayment by time horizon and option value. Great Eastern was poor for its original commercial objective yet later uniquely valuable for cable work; additional complexity can fail its declared objective while retaining future reuse value. Cost/value accounting must bind goal and horizon.",
    "S7": "HD2 strengthens but also narrows metaproductivity: telegraph, dynamo, spectroscopy, rail and long-term experiments alter future production/discovery capacity, yet guano/rail colonial systems and labor regimes show that capability growth is not net social value."
  },
